  "body": "Archive the reviewed camera bit/XSA, original BD/XDC and required IP inputs with SHA256 provenance, isolated project creation and standalone sources.\n\nAdd the Linux DMA driver, capture/JPEG workers, browser MJPEG controls, PC loopback viewer, guarded SD recovery/install/load tooling and validated AArch64 binaries. Preserve historical ELF archives as separate profiles.\n\nDocument each component, deployment and restart steps, measured results, licenses and remaining limits; keep system images and credentials local.\n\nValidation: SD Python 9 tests and PowerShell 12 guard cases; standalone rebuild; Python/PowerShell/shell/Tcl checks; archive/deployment hashes. Hardware evidence: one SD cold boot, direct SSH/SCP, 600-second CAM0 capture, stale/kill/restart handling and 757 full-size JPEGs at 25.16 received fps. Matching Vivado 2020.2 synthesis was not rerun; hand control remains pending.",
